ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":176,"prev":178,"next":181,"titles":183,"firmware":45},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":20,"status":21,"firmware":22,"facts":29,"procedures":90,"parameters":135,"related":152,"body":157,"sources":158,"official_url":33,"controls":169},"com.midi-settings","MIDI settings",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"midi setup","midi clock settings","clock in","clock out","midi echo","midi thru","active track channel","transport sync","com",20,"knowledge/manual/units/com/midi-settings.md",{"modes":17,"screens":18},[],[13,19],"system settings","The midi section of the system settings sets, separately for clock, notes and everything else, whether the OP-XY listens, transmits or does both; it also picks the channel that always plays the selected track and switches echo on or off.","current",{"min":23,"changed_in":24,"guide_version":27,"verified_on":28},"1.0.9",[25,26,27],"1.0.15","1.0.29","1.1.15",null,[30,35,38,41,47,50,55,58,61,64,67,71,74,78,82,86],{"id":31,"text":32,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"location","The MIDI options are one section of the system settings, reached with `com → M1`.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/com#system-settings","official",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"five-settings","The section has five settings: clock, notes, other (every remaining message type), active track channel and midi echo.",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"active-track","Notes arriving on the active track channel play whichever track is currently selected.",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"stock-values","On a unit with stock settings (OS 1.1.33) the section reads: clock in, notes both, other both, active track channel 1, midi echo off.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133","1.1.33","verified",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"directions","Clock, notes and other each take a direction; in (receive only) and both (receive and send) are confirmed on OS 1.1.33.",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":53,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":54},"more-directions","Community tools also describe out (send only) and off for these three settings.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#91-settings-that-gate-midi","community",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"clock-in-silent","With clock set to in, pressing `play` or `stop` sends nothing — no start, no stop, no clock ticks.",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"clock-both-transport","With clock set to both, every press of `play` sends a MIDI start (FA) — a press during playback sends another start — and `stop` sends a MIDI stop (FC). No continue (FB) or song position (F2) messages were seen.",{"id":62,"text":63,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"clock-both-ticks","With clock set to both, clock ticks (F8, 24 per quarter note) stream all the time, even while stopped.",{"id":65,"text":66,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"transport-in","With clock set to both, a start (FA) or stop (FC) from a computer starts or stops playback, and the unit sends the message back out.",{"id":68,"text":69,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":70},"follow-apps","Software that follows the OP-XY's play state and tempo over USB, this app included, needs clock set to both.","derived",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"sysex-returns","Even with midi echo off, a universal identity request (SysEx) sent to the unit came back on its output; what forwards it is not known yet.",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":77,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"echo-linked","OS 1.0.15 fixed the echo setting being ignored for notes from linked tracks.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.15",{"id":79,"text":80,"source":81,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"transport-relay","Start and stop received from one device are passed on to the other connected MIDI devices.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.28",{"id":83,"text":84,"source":85,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"monitor","A monitor page in the same settings lists whatever MIDI arrives — channel, value, clock and SysEx — which tells a message that never arrived from one that arrived but was ignored.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/com#midi-monitor",{"id":87,"text":88,"source":89,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"per-device","Switches for what is sent to and received from each connected device live separately, under `com → M3` (devices).","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/com#devices",[91,101,113,126],{"id":92,"goal":93,"preconditions":94,"steps":95,"result":28,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"open","Open the MIDI settings",[],[96,98],{"keys":97,"note":19,"set":28},"com → M1",{"keys":99,"note":100,"set":28},"turn E1","choose the midi section",{"id":102,"goal":103,"preconditions":104,"steps":106,"result":28,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"change","Change one MIDI setting",[105],"the midi section is open",[107,110],{"keys":108,"note":109,"set":28},"turn E2","pick the setting",{"keys":111,"note":112,"set":28},"turn E3","set its value (`turn E4` works too)",{"id":114,"goal":115,"preconditions":116,"steps":117,"result":125,"source":44,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":45,"confidence":46},"send-clock","Make the OP-XY send transport and clock over MIDI",[],[118,119,121,123],{"keys":97,"note":28,"set":28},{"keys":99,"note":120,"set":28},"midi section",{"keys":108,"note":122,"set":28},"clock",{"keys":111,"note":124,"set":28},"both","`play` and `stop` now send start and stop, and clock ticks run continuously.",{"id":127,"goal":128,"preconditions":129,"steps":131,"result":134,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"leave","Leave the system settings",[130],"the system settings are open",[132],{"keys":133,"note":28,"set":28},"M1","Back on the com page.",[136,141,145,148],{"screen":19,"encoder":137,"layer":138,"keys":99,"name":139,"range":28,"default":28,"cc":28,"cc_confidence":28,"note":140,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"E1","base","section","system, keyboard, midi, clock, pitchbend, battery, monitor",{"screen":19,"encoder":142,"layer":138,"keys":108,"name":143,"range":28,"default":28,"cc":28,"cc_confidence":28,"note":144,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"E2","setting","the setting within the section",{"screen":19,"encoder":146,"layer":138,"keys":111,"name":147,"range":28,"default":28,"cc":28,"cc_confidence":28,"note":28,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"E3","value",{"screen":19,"encoder":149,"layer":138,"keys":150,"name":147,"range":28,"default":28,"cc":28,"cc_confidence":28,"note":151,"source":33,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":28,"confidence":34},"E4","turn E4","same as `E3`",[153,154,155,156],"com.midi-monitor","com.devices","com.midi-cc-reference","hardware.layout","The midi section is where the OP-XY decides how it talks to other gear. Clock, notes and \"other\"\n(every remaining message type, such as control changes) each get a direction, so the unit can, say,\ntake notes from a keyboard while ignoring its clock. The active track channel is a shortcut for playing\nthe OP-XY from a controller: whatever arrives on that channel plays the track you have selected.\n\nOut of the box the unit only listens for clock (clock in), so it sends no start, stop or clock of\nits own. Switching clock to both makes it a sync source: `play` and `stop` send start and stop, and\nthe tick stream runs continuously. This app suggests clock both during setup so it can follow the\nunit's transport and tempo.\n\nWhen a connection misbehaves, open the monitor page first: it shows whether a message reached the\nOP-XY at all. Per-device switches live separately in `com → M3`.",[159,161,163,164,166,167,168],{"url":33,"kind":160},"guide",{"url":44,"kind":162},"research",{"url":53,"kind":162},{"url":77,"kind":165},"changelog",{"url":81,"kind":165},{"url":85,"kind":160},{"url":89,"kind":160},[170,171,172,173,174,175],"key.com","key.m1","encoder.1","encoder.2","encoder.3","encoder.4",{"id":13,"title":177},"Connectivity",{"id":179,"title":180},"com.system-settings-os12","System settings on OS 1.2",{"id":153,"title":182},"MIDI monitor",{"basics.key-notation":184,"basics.main-modes":185,"basics.modules":186,"basics.track-buttons":187,"basics.linked-tracks":188,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":189,"basics.workflow":190,"basics.firmware-versions":191,"hardware.layout":192,"hardware.power-and-charging":193,"hardware.connectors":194,"hardware.specifications":195,"hardware.te-boot":196,"hardware.firmware-update":197,"hardware.factory-reset":198,"hardware.system-menu":199,"hardware.safety-and-care":200,"hardware.in-the-box":201,"sequencer.overview":202,"sequencer.step-entry":203,"sequencer.step-recording":204,"sequencer.live-recording":205,"sequencer.extend-notes":206,"sequencer.nudge":207,"sequencer.single-sound":208,"sequencer.rotate":209,"sequencer.copy-step":210,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":211,"sequencer.parameter-locks":212,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":213,"sequencer.step-components":214,"sequencer.step-component-reference":215,"sequencer.component-pulse":216,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":217,"sequencer.component-multiply":218,"sequencer.component-velocity":219,"sequencer.component-ramp-up":220,"sequencer.component-ramp-down":221,"sequencer.component-random":222,"sequencer.component-portamento":223,"sequencer.component-bend":224,"sequ